                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_26\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit moves `mContainerView.removeView(removedPage.getView())` and `mCurPage = prevPage` out of `doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal` (which only runs after the pop animation finishes, via a `postDelayed` Runnable, when the pop is animated) and into `popPageInternal` itself, so they execute immediately when a page is popped, regardless of whether a transition animation is playing. The fix commit message states: \"mCurPage should be set to null immediately when last page is popped, even if there is a transition animation to play.\"\n\nBefore candidate_26, `popPageInternal` set `mCurPage = prevPage` synchronously/immediately, right after computing `prevPage`, before scheduling any animation-related `postDelayed` callback. This was correct behavior.\n\ncandidate_26 refactors `popPageInternal` by extracting the removal/cleanup logic (`mContainerView.removeView(removedPage.getView())`, `removedPage.onDetach()`, `removedPage.onHidden()`, `mCurPage = prevPage`, and `prevPage.onUncovered(...)`) into a new private method `doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal(Page removedPage, Page prevPage)`. Crucially, this new method is invoked either immediately (no animation) or, when animated, only inside the `postDelayed` Runnable that runs after `animationDuration` has elapsed. This means `mCurPage` is no longer updated immediately when popping the last page \u2014 it stays stale until the animation completes, which is precisely the bug the fix corrects: \"mCurPage should be set to null immediately when last page is popped, even if there is a transition animation to play.\"\n\nThis is a direct structural match: the fix essentially reverses candidate_26's refactor by hoisting `mContainerView.removeView(...)` and `mCurPage = prevPage` back out of the animation-gated `doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal` call and placing them before the animation-duration check in `popPageInternal`. No other candidate introduces or modifies the `doFinalWorkForPopPageInternal` method or this delayed-assignment pattern for `mCurPage`.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
